  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A warm travel journal",
    "overview": "Cream paper, forest ink, editorial serif headings and destination photography establish the implemented direction delegated by the user. Local Manrope gives navigation, forms and metadata a practical voice. This document records the current implementation in `client/src/style.css` and `client/src/App.jsx`, checked against `.local/ui/desktop.png` and `.local/ui/mobile.png`; it does not introduce a new visual identity.\n\nThe landing page works in Persuade mode: generous space, a large invitation, destination search and a photographic introduction. Discovery, trip details, editing, profiles and chat work in Operate mode: clear controls, visible state, compact metadata and task-oriented layouts. Keep the shared palette and typography while respecting that difference in density.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm cream and forest green, with restrained sage and copper accents.",
      "Serif editorial hierarchy paired with local Manrope controls.",
      "Destination photographs and open, unboxed trip cards.",
      "Responsive forms and explicit loading, empty, error and demo states."
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the cream canvas, forest hierarchy and serif/Manrope pairing.",
      "Do preserve visible labels, focus states, responsive stacking and clear asynchronous feedback.",
      "Do identify demonstration itineraries wherever they appear."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't enclose every trip in a raised white card.",
      "Don't repeat the hero curve or rotated note on ordinary application controls.",
      "Don't trade operational clarity for landing-page decoration.\r"
    ]
  }
}
